'''Darts D'Nar '''was a [[Gender|male]] [[Zygerrian]] who worked with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and his [[Zygerria|homeworld's]] [[Zygerrian Slave Empire|slave Empire]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Allied with [[Count]] [[Dooku]], he [[Conquest of Kiros|led]] Separatist forces to the [[planet]] [[Kiros]] and instrumented the kidnapping of a [[Artisan colony|colony]] of [[Togruta]]. When [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] forces arrived, D'Nar fought against [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] until his plans to detonate bombs around the city were foiled by Kenobi's Jedi companions, [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Ahsoka Tano]]. D'Nar attempted to flee in [[Tecora|his ship]], but was caught by Skywalker and Tano.

==Biography==
{{Quote|You've broken through my defenses. You think you've won. Think again.|Darts D'Nar, to Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Kidnapped" />}}
[[File:DookuDnarArriveOnKiros-Kidnapped.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Darts D'Nar arrives on Kiros along with Separatist forces.]]
Darts D'Nar was a [[Gender|male]] [[Zygerrian]] who was a part of the [[Zygerrian Slave Empire]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], D'Nar allied with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and accompanied his [[Unidentified T-series tactical droid (Kiros)|tactical droid]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]], and their [[battle droid]]s to [[Kiros]]. After Dooku spoke with its [[governor]], [[Gupat Roshti]], D'Nar ordered his [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|tactical droid]] to [[Conquest of Kiros|round up]] all the citizens of a [[Togruta]] [[Artisan colony|colony]]. D'Nar then stayed inside the [[governor's tower]], collecting [[Kiros bird|birds]]. Ten cycles after his round-up, he and his forces came under [[Battle on Kiros|attack]] by the [[Galactic Republic]] under [[Jedi General]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], and Commander [[Ahsoka Tano]]. D'Nar then contacted [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody]] and invited Kenobi into the tower to negotiate the terms of surrender.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

[[File:KenobiDNarFight.png|thumb|right|260px|D'Nar fights Obi-Wan Kenobi.]]
D'Nar spoke with Count Dooku and Zygerrian [[Prime Minister]] [[Atai Molec]] about the last slave shipment and assured them that he would deal with [[Jedi]]. As Kenobi arrived, D'Nar was ordered by Dooku to bring Kenobi to him on his knees. D'Nar then told Kenobi that is he who would surrender. At first, Kenobi refused, but D'Nar revealed he had planted several bombs around the city in various buildings and threatened to blow them up if he did not surrender. Kenobi, knowing that Skywalker and his apprentice were listening, agreed with D'Nar's demands and surrendered his lightsaber to him. D'Nar then told Kenobi that he would punish him for what the Jedi did to his people's slave empire, but Dooku would displeased. Kenobi then offered to fight him in the Zygerrian way, agreeing to surrender if D'Nar were to win, an offer the Zygerrian accepted. D'Nar fought Kenobi until his tactical droid informed that Skywalker had defused all of his bombs. Refusing to surrender, D'Nar then activated a bomb on his tactical droid's back and threw the droid at Kenobi, knocking the Jedi over and giving him time to make his escape.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

D'Nar scrambled to to his ship, the ''[[Tecora]]'', as he was being pursued by Skywalker and Tano. As he took off, D'Nar's ship was then crippled. When he saw the Jedi, D'Nar unleashed his pet [[blixus]] upon them. D'Nar was then confronted by Tano in the ship's cockpit. He fought her using his [[electro-whip]], but was subdued by her. Skywalker then questioned him as to the location of the missing colonists. At first, D'Nar refused and taunted the two Jedi, but conceded and told Skywalker when he was threatened with the Jedi's [[Skywalker lightsaber|lightsaber]], revealing that his [[Miraj Scintel|Queen]] would be auctioning off the colonists to bring back their empire.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:DartsDNar-TCWCEJtB.png|thumb|right|200px|D'Nar was ruthless and cruel]]
{{Quote|Zygerria will be rich and powerful again. The Jedi will not stop us this time.|Darts D'Nar|<ref name="Kidnapped" />}}
Darts D'Nar was male<ref name="Databank" /> Zygerrian<ref name="Kidnapped" /> who was 1.89 [[meter]]s, or 6 [[Foot|feet]], 2 inches tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|brown]] [[hair]] that was graying, silver [[eye]]s and gray skin. He was a ruthless Zygerrian commander and slaver, determined to restore the slave empire to its former glory. He was a decent fighter in [[Unarmed combat|hand-to-hand combat]], dealing out multiple punishing blows when fighting against Obi-Wan Kenobi. D'Nar was also considerably strong, at one point tossing Kenobi a fair distance across a room. However, he did not realize the Jedi was stalling, so his allies could diffuse the bombs set by the Zygerrians. D'Nar did not have much respect for the lives of others, working in a slave empire. In addition to enslaving [[Sentience|sentient]] beings, he also sold various animals as pets.<ref name="Kidnapped" /> 

==Skills and abilities==
D'Nar was a decent fighter in combat,<ref name="Kidnapped" /> and was also experienced in military tactics, security and as a leader.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
D'Nar used an electro-whip in combat. He also wore traditional Zygerrian attire.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

==Behind the scenes==
D'Nar first appeared in the episode "[[Kidnapped]]," the eleventh episode of the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' television series']] [[The Clone Wars: Season Four|fourth season]]. He was voiced by [[Nick Jameson]].

